WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.723
Null if is another simple but useful SQL function It
compares two

00:00:05.748 --> 00:00:11.420
expressions If they are equal it returns null
Otherwise it

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:15.969
returns the first expression On this slide we use B
trim to

00:00:15.995 --> 00:00:20.621
remove spaces around an email address Then null if
converts an empty

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:27.429
string into null This helps us normalize text before
later logic There

00:00:27.454 --> 00:00:31.915
is a runnable example below Click Run in the browser
and compare

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.910
the original email with the normalized email Then if
you want to

00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:41.974
practice in PostgreSQL directly click Copy open
pgAdmin and run the query

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.551
in the Query Tool Pay special attention to records
containing blank or

00:00:46.576 --> 00:00:51.447
whitespace-only text Those are the records where
this pattern is most useful
